e, though the state's Republican fundamentals keep this well short of Likely D.", "watch": "A late Paxton rescue via the $131 million outside spending campaign, or a turnout shift among low-propensity Republican voters, could close the polling gap before Election Day.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: John Cornyn (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Texas's open Senate seat features Democrat James Talarico against Republican Ken Paxton after Paxton defeated the incumbent in a renomination fight. Polls through early October consistently show Talarico ahead, with high-quality surveys from YouGov and NYT/Siena giving him a six-point lead and the overall average around three points. Prediction markets price Talarico's chances near two-thirds, and most expert ratings land at Tossup or a slight Democratic lean.\nPaxton faces heavy outside opposition spending and reported internal campaign friction, while Talarico holds an enormous cash advantage. Still, Texas's Republican-leaning fundamentals and a large Libertarian candidate on the ballot add uncertainty, making this a genuine but modest Democratic edge rather than a safe seat.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6697, "margin": 2.08}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6924, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7255, "margin": 2.8}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6997, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6523, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6444, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6983, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7151, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.701, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7008, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.6832, "margin": 2.2}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7125, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7022, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.6597, "margin": 2.6}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.6724, "